sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    actor Steward
    participant Page as Web pages<br/>site page, admin site page,<br/>new-report
    participant Api as Image delete route<br/>(proposed)
    participant Server as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase DB<br/>attachments,<br/>homepage_image_uploads
    participant S3 as AWS S3

    Note over Admin,S3: Covers US 7.0.5. No image delete exists today, and no code deletes S3 objects.<br/>"(proposed)" = the step is not in the code today.

    Note over Admin,S3: Delete an image (AT 1, AT 2, AT 3)
    Admin->>Page: Open a site gallery. It shows attachments images (/api/sites/[siteId]/gallery)<br/>and homepage_image_uploads images (/api/homepage-images/[siteId]). Both exist.
    Page->>Page: Show Delete only to Admins (AT 2) (proposed)
    Admin->>Page: Select Delete on an image and confirm (proposed)
    Page->>Api: DELETE with image kind (inspection attachment<br/>or homepage upload) and image id (proposed)
    Api->>Api: Check caller is Admin from a trusted role source, store not decided
    alt Caller is not Admin (AT 2)
        Api-->>Page: 403. Nothing is deleted
    else Caller is Admin
        Api->>DB: Read storage_key from the table of that image kind:<br/>attachments or homepage_image_uploads
        DB-->>Api: storage_key
        Api->>S3: DeleteObject(storage_key) (AT 3)
        alt S3 delete fails
            S3-->>Api: Error
            Api-->>Page: Error. Row is kept
        else File is deleted
            S3-->>Api: OK
            Api->>DB: Delete that row from the same table
            Api-->>Page: Success
            Page-->>Admin: Image is gone from gallery and reports (AT 1)
        end
    end
    Note over Api,S3: Open questions: the order (S3 object first, then the row, as shown)<br/>and a retry when one of the two deletes fails.

    Note over Admin,S3: Deactivate a SIR (AT 4): this exists and keeps the files
    Admin->>Page: Deactivate a SIR on the admin site page
    Page->>Server: setFormResponseActive(responseId, false)
    Server->>DB: Set is_active false on form_responses
    Note over Server,S3: Attachment rows and S3 files stay, so reactivation restores the photos.

    Note over Admin,S3: Failed SIR submission (AT 5)
    Steward->>Page: Submit new SIR with photos
    Page->>S3: PUT photos to inspections/{siteId}/{responseId}/ (exists)
    Page->>Server: uploadSiteInspectionAnswers or<br/>insertInspectionAttachments fails
    Page->>Server: rollbackSiteInspectionSubmission(responseId) (exists)
    Server->>DB: Delete attachment, answer and response rows (exists)
    Server->>S3: Delete all objects under inspections/{siteId}/{responseId}/ (proposed)
    Page-->>Steward: Show error. SIR is not saved
    Note over Server,S3: Today rollback deletes only database rows. The uploaded files stay in S3.
